usb: typec: ucsi: retry re-enabling notifications after resume

On the Dell XPS 13 9350 (2024, Lunar Lake) the PPM does not respond to
UCSI_SET_NOTIFICATION_ENABLE for several seconds after s2idle resume:
every single resume logs

  ucsi_acpi USBC000:00: failed to re-enable notifications (-110)

exactly one command timeout after "PM: suspend exit" (20/20 resumes in
the journal of one boot). ucsi_resume_work() gives up on the first
failure, leaving the notification mask disabled and skipping the
connector re-check.

Retry the command a couple of times before giving up. Each attempt
already blocks for the command timeout, so this adds no delay in the
success case and only bounded extra wait when the PPM is slow to wake.

--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
index 49f1c53721bb..c1517a0a46ef 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
@@ -2159,16 +2159,25 @@ static void ucsi_resume_work(struct work_struct *work)
 {
 	struct ucsi *ucsi = container_of(work, struct ucsi, resume_work);
 	struct ucsi_connector *con;
+	unsigned int attempts = 0;
 	u64 command;
 	int ret;
 
 	/* Restore UCSI notification enable mask after system resume */
 	command = UCSI_SET_NOTIFICATION_ENABLE | ucsi->ntfy;
-	ret = ucsi_send_command(ucsi, command, NULL, 0);
-	if (ret < 0) {
-		dev_err(ucsi->dev, "failed to re-enable notifications (%d)\n", ret);
-		return;
-	}
+	do {
+		ret = ucsi_send_command(ucsi, command, NULL, 0);
+		if (ret >= 0)
+			break;
+		/*
+		 * Some PPMs take seconds after s2idle resume to accept
+		 * commands; each attempt already waits the command timeout.
+		 */
+		if (ret != -ETIMEDOUT || ++attempts == 3) {
+			dev_err(ucsi->dev, "failed to re-enable notifications (%d)\n", ret);
+			return;
+		}
+	} while (true);
 
 	for (con = ucsi->connector; con->port; con++) {
 		mutex_lock(&con->lock);
